<title>BELGIUM: EU confirms Belgian green rate to devalue Thursday.</title>
<headline>EU confirms Belgian green rate to devalue Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rate of the Belgian franc will be devalued on Thursday to 39.6918 per Ecu, from 39.6411, in the European Union's agrimonetary grid, the European Commission confirmed.</p>
<p>The U.K. Home-Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) earlier on Wednesday forecast the devaluation, triggered by the renewed strength of sterling.</p>
<p>Green rates are used to calculate EU farm subsidies and intervention prices in national currencies.</p>
</text>
